subproblem.statement:
Let P, n ∈ ℕ, U ⊆ ℝ^P and Z ∈ 𝒟_n(U), and let R = (M, θ, ξ) be an IMRep in U (contract structure IMRep U n) representing Z. That is, Z(ω) = R.action(ω) = ∫_M θ(x)⟨ω(x), ξ(x)⟩ dHⁿ(x) for every ω ∈ 𝒟ⁿ(U), where Hⁿ = μHE[n] and ⟨ω(x), ξ(x)⟩ = ξ(x)(ω(x)). Let R.measure = (Hⁿ⌞M).withDensity θ. Then:
(a) R.measure(K) < ∞ for every compact K ⊆ U;
(b) ξ is R.measure-a.e. strongly measurable;
(c) if for Hⁿ⌞M-a.e. x one has |⟨α, ξ(x)⟩| ≤ |α| for every n-covector α (|α| = covectorEuclideanNorm α), then the same holds for R.measure-a.e. x;
(d) Z(ω) = ∫ ⟨ω(x), ξ(x)⟩ dR.measure(x) for every ω ∈ 𝒟ⁿ(U).
